{"term":"risk","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4211d4f156f9b9d319","definition":"The probability of a negative outcome to a decision or event.","example":"There is risk of being brutalized, arrested, imprisoned and tortured, all because I want you to know the truth about this matter.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["assigned risk","assumption of risk","at any risk","at one's own risk","at one's risk","at risk","at the risk of","businessman's risk","calculated risk","country risk","credit risk","currency risk","cyberrisk","derisk","diversifiable risk","exchange rate risk","existential risk","external risk","extreme risk law","extreme risk protection order","financial risk","flight risk","foreign exchange risk","funding liquidity risk","FX risk","georisk","health risk","high-risk","ikigai risk","inflation risk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e9f602b2df8d9c367e","definition":"The magnitude of possible loss consequent to a decision or event.","example":"Will they find the prospect of greater risk a cause for concern, rather than a gift from the right?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["assigned risk","assumption of risk","at any risk","at one's own risk","at one's risk","at risk","at the risk of","businessman's risk","calculated risk","country risk","credit risk","currency risk","cyberrisk","derisk","diversifiable risk","exchange rate risk","existential risk","external risk","extreme risk law","extreme risk protection order","financial risk","flight risk","foreign exchange risk","funding liquidity risk","FX risk","georisk","health risk","high-risk","ikigai risk","inflation risk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:992d65d14e1a2672d5","definition":"The potential negative effect of an event, determined by multiplying the likelihood of the event occurring with its magnitude should it occur.","example":"If there is a 25% chance of running over schedule, costing you a $100 out of your own pocket, that might be a risk you are willing to take. But if you have a 5% chance of running overschedule, knowing that there is a $10,000 penalty, you might be less willing to take that risk.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["assigned risk","assumption of risk","at any risk","at one's own risk","at one's risk","at risk","at the risk of","businessman's risk","calculated risk","country risk","credit risk","currency risk","cyberrisk","derisk","diversifiable risk","exchange rate risk","existential risk","external risk","extreme risk law","extreme risk protection order","financial risk","flight risk","foreign exchange risk","funding liquidity risk","FX risk","georisk","health risk","high-risk","ikigai risk","inflation risk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2b4f9f90913393aa3d","definition":"A possible adverse event or outcome.","example":"the imminent and constant risk of assassination, a risk which has shaken very strong nerves","pos":"noun","synonyms":["danger","peril","hazard"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["assigned risk","assumption of risk","at any risk","at one's own risk","at one's risk","at risk","at the risk of","businessman's risk","calculated risk","country risk","credit risk","currency risk","cyberrisk","derisk","diversifiable risk","exchange rate risk","existential risk","external risk","extreme risk law","e